<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>Who an estimate review is for</h2>
<p>An estimate review fits property owners who have the carrier’s estimate in hand and a feeling that something is wrong, but no clear picture of what or how much. It also fits contractors and public adjusters who want an independent read before advising a client to invoke appraisal.</p>
<h2>What we check</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Scope.</strong> Are all damaged areas, elevations and rooms included? Are tear-out, detach-and-reset and cleanup listed?</li>
<li><strong>Quantities.</strong> Do roof squares, wall areas and flooring measurements match the building?</li>
<li><strong>Pricing.</strong> Are unit prices current for your Illinois market, and are labor minimums applied?</li>
<li><strong>Code items.</strong> Are local code requirements such as ice-and-water shield, drip edge and electrical upgrades addressed?</li>
<li><strong>Depreciation and O&amp;P.</strong> Is depreciation reasonable and applied only where the policy allows? Is overhead and profit included where multiple trades are involved?</li>
</ul>
<h2>What you get</h2>
<p>A written summary listing each gap, why it matters and an approximate value, plus our honest recommendation: request a supplement, invoke appraisal, or accept the estimate. If the problem is really a coverage question, we say so and suggest you talk to an attorney.</p>
<h2>Why start here</h2>
<p>Appraisal has real costs. A review keeps you from spending them on a small or weak gap, and it gives you a solid foundation if appraisal does make sense. If you hire us as your appraiser afterward, the review work carries straight into the valuation.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I need my contractor’s estimate for a review?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>It helps, but it isn’t required. We can review the carrier’s estimate against photos and measurements alone.</p></div></details><details><summary>Will the carrier know I had a review done?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Only if you share it. Many clients use the review to support a supplement request.</p></div></details></div>
